.nh
.TH "CITADEL" "1" "Sep 2026" "AceTeam" "Citadel CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
citadel-module-restart - Restart a single module: stop then start it (scoped)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcitadel module restart  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Restarts one module by name -- equivalent to 'citadel module stop \&'
immediately followed by 'citadel module start \&'. No other module is
touched and the worker is not restarted.

.PP
Add --dry-run to preview what would happen (resolved node dir, compose file,
container(s)) without doing it. Add --expect-node  to refuse the
action (fail closed) unless the resolved node's identity matches -- a safety
check for scripted/agent use against a specific node.

.PP
This IS the blessed recovery path for a stopped/crashed service, embedded
engine (vllm, bonsai, unlimited-ocr, ...) or catalog module alike -- never
hand-run 'docker compose up' directly.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Print what would happen (resolved node dir, compose file, container(s)) without doing it

.PP
\fB--expect-node\fP=""
	Refuse to act unless the resolved node's identity (name, hostname, or mesh ID) matches this value

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for restart


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug output

.PP
\fB--no-auto-update\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic update checks and installs for this run (or set CITADEL_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colorized output

.PP
\fB--node-dir\fP=""
	Override the node config directory (citadel.yaml + services/), bypassing $HOME/ConfigDir resolution. Also settable via CITADEL_NODE_DIR. Scope: manifest/services resolution only -- does NOT redirect network state, the module lockfile, or nodevault.

.PP
\fB--runtime\fP=""
	Container runtime for module containers: docker or podman (default: auto-detect)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  citadel module restart vllm
  citadel module restart vllm --dry-run
  citadel module restart vllm --expect-node my-test-node
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcitadel-module(1)\fP
